WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.231
"Finally, PE!" Briana began doing warm-up stretches.

2
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:12.619
"I wonder what we'll do today," Ally said.

3
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.085
It had been too snowy for the past month to hold PE outside.

4
00:00:17.086 --> 00:00:22.617
"I don't care. Anything is better than history class," Briana said.

5
00:00:22.618 --> 00:00:25.581
"It's so boring!"

6
00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:34.978
Mrs. Farrow, the PE teacher, entered the gymnasium carrying two large trash cans and a soccer ball.

7
00:00:34.979 --> 00:00:39.496
"Are we playing soccer inside?" Miguel asked hopefully.

8
00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:44.014
"That doesn't explain the trash cans," Briana said.

9
00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:49.870
Mrs. Farrow grinned. "We are having a history lesson!"

10
00:00:49.871 --> 00:00:56.509
"No! Not history!" Briana moaned.

11
00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.423
Mrs. Farrow ignored the complaint.

12
00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:04.900
"It was a snowy winter in Massachusetts in 1891," she began.

13
00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:08.421
"Too snowy for baseball or football.

14
00:01:08.422 --> 00:01:16.874
A group of college students was stuck inside for every PE class, so their teacher invented a new game for them to play.

15
00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:20.918
Today we're going to play that game!"

16
00:01:20.919 --> 00:01:26.705
"This might be better than regular history class," Briana thought.

17
00:01:26.706 --> 00:01:31.737
"The teacher's name was James Naismith," Mrs. Farrow said.

18
00:01:31.738 --> 00:01:37.307
"He based his idea on a throwing game from his childhood in Canada.

19
00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:43.804
The targets he decided on were peach baskets, but these are the best I can do."

20
00:01:43.805 --> 00:01:49.644
She gestured to the trash cans. "Now, to get them in place."

21
00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:55.619
The custodian brought a ladder and fastened a trash can high on the gym wall.

22
00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.892
The kids laughed at the sight.

23
00:02:00.893 --> 00:02:09.300
As the custodian put another trash can on the opposite wall, Mrs. Farrow divided the students into teams of nine.

24
00:02:09.301 --> 00:02:16.219
"The point of the game is to get the ball into your opposing team's trash can," Mrs. Farrow explained.

25
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.525
"You cannot run with the ball or touch the other players.

26
00:02:20.526 --> 00:02:24.423
Whichever team scores the most goals wins."

27
00:02:24.424 --> 00:02:28.068
"That sounds like basketball," Briana said.

28
00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:31.932
"Exactly!" Mrs. Farrow said.

29
00:02:31.933 --> 00:02:36.563
"But why do you have a soccer ball?" Ally asked.

30
00:02:36.564 --> 00:02:42.064
"Early basketball players used soccer balls," the teacher answered.

31
00:02:42.065 --> 00:02:46.530
"Real basketballs weren't made until 1894.

32
00:02:46.531 --> 00:02:50.014
They were made from leather and stitched together." She

33
00:02:50.015 --> 00:02:55.024
patted the soccer ball. "Ready for the tip-off?" Briana

34
00:02:55.025 --> 00:02:57.624
faced off against Miguel. Basketball

35
00:02:57.625 --> 00:03:03.403
was her favorite game, but she never thought it had any connection to history! The

36
00:03:03.404 --> 00:03:07.692
teacher tossed the ball high, and both kids leaped for it. Briana

37
00:03:07.693 --> 00:03:11.842
made contact first, sending the ball straight to Ally. Ally

38
00:03:11.843 --> 00:03:20.488
dribbled— tweet! The whistle sounded.

39
00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:26.497
"I forgot to mention dribbling the ball wasn't allowed until 1909," Mrs. Farrow said.

40
00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:32.667
"The only way to move the ball is to pass it to someone else."

41
00:03:32.668 --> 00:03:34.077
They started again.

42
00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:39.753
Briana caught a pass from Kevin, the soccer ball feeling strangely soft and light in her hands.

43
00:03:39.754 --> 00:03:42.489
She shot the ball over Miguel's head.

44
00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.877
It clanged into the trash can.

45
00:03:44.878 --> 00:03:47.497
Ally gave her a high five.

46
00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:51.208
"You're better at history than you thought!"

47
00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:54.281
"First goal!" Mrs. Farrow said.

48
00:03:54.282 --> 00:03:59.897
"Now we just need to get the ball back . . . "

49
00:03:59.898 --> 00:04:04.571
The players waited while the teacher climbed the ladder and retrieved the ball.

50
00:04:04.572 --> 00:04:08.501
"Don't make too many goals!" the teacher joked.

51
00:04:08.502 --> 00:04:15.601
"Real baskets are definitely better than trash cans—or peach baskets!" Briana said.

52
00:04:15.602 --> 00:04:20.571
After another fifteen minutes, Miguel's team was in the lead by one goal.

53
00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:25.751
Mrs. Farrow blew her whistle again to signal the end of play.

54
00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:29.408
"Whew!" Briana was breathing hard but grinning.

55
00:04:29.409 --> 00:04:31.994
"That was a good game."

56
00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:35.057
Mrs. Farrow gathered the class together.

57
00:04:35.058 --> 00:04:38.108
"What do you think of old-school basketball?"

58
00:04:38.109 --> 00:04:41.871
"It's hard not to dribble the ball," Miguel said.

59
00:04:41.872 --> 00:04:46.813
"And it's strange to have more than five on a team," Ally added.

60
00:04:46.814 --> 00:04:50.863
"A lot is the same though," Briana said.

61
00:04:50.864 --> 00:04:56.480
"Making baskets, passing the ball, not touching the other players . . . "

62
00:04:56.481 --> 00:04:58.687
The teacher nodded.

63
00:04:58.688 --> 00:05:05.482
"Mr. Naismith wanted to make a game that was all about skill and strategy, not force."

64
00:05:05.483 --> 00:05:07.418
Briana smiled.

65
00:05:07.419 --> 00:05:13.145
"I still prefer modern basketball. But the old-school game was fun."

66
00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:17.135
"Does that mean you like history now?" Mrs. Farrow asked.

67
00:05:17.136 --> 00:05:23.636
Briana laughed. "Not exactly!"

